id: pm-gh1631
title: "GH-1631: expose bounded extension-owned diagnostics on expected SDK errors"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1631 requests a namespaced JSON-compatible extension diagnostics slot on PmCliErrorContext and createPmCliExpectedError. Its concrete producer is pm-changelog issue 302: selection_report loses structure through host-owned prose fields. Design typed SDK and CLI/TOON/JSON contracts with size bounds and explicit exclusion from telemetry/Sentry; avoid widening arbitrary error payload capture."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T22:37:34.363Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T06:09:24.558Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:47.660Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T21:06:47.660Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Cover public SDK typing and separately bundled expected errors; preserve nested safe JSON diagnostics in JSON and TOON; enforce bounded output and prove telemetry/Sentry exclusion with real local collectors; coordinate pm-changelog producer adoption in its own repository.
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: "PmCliErrorContext.details with SDK admission (TypeError on malformed shapes), whole-or-receipt rendering within PM_CLI_ERROR_DETAILS_LIMITS in JSON, text and MCP, and exclusion from telemetry classification and Sentry payloads."
expected_result: "Extensions return structured refusal facts through a documented SDK field, bounded deterministically and never sent to telemetry or Sentry."
actual_result: "A separately bundled refusal's details reach JSON and text output whole under Node and Bun, oversized payloads become details_omitted receipts, and real local OTLP and Sentry collectors never receive the payload."
dependencies[3]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
